  "problem": "${(7\\cdot 9)}^{4}\\cdot {7}^{6}=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the second factor using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n{(7\\cdot 9)}^{4}\\cdot {7}^{6}={7}^{4}\\cdot {9}^{4}\\cdot {7}^{6}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule for exponents, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{4}\\cdot {9}^{4}\\cdot {7}^{6} & ={9}^{4}\\cdot {7}^{4}\\cdot {7}^{6} \\\\  & ={9}^{4}\\cdot {7}^{4+6} \\\\  & ={9}^{4}\\cdot {7}^{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
